I finally gave in to temptation, now when I play a
Valkerie in NetHack, the absurd32.bmp file I created
has Britney Spears in her valkerie costume as the
tile. I'm slowly working on creating the other,
larger sizes.

Doing so is a bit awkward, because you want the
background to _exactly_ match all the other tiles,
otherwise she looks like she's dragging a private
piece of floor around with her (the truth) rather
than stepping onto the next grid location, the
desired fantasy effect. This means you have to open
each separate size bitmap and grab its floor tile,
you can't just grab one and scale it up or down.

The larger bitmaps are _massive_ files.

At 32x32 There's no way you'd recognize her, of
course, but at 128x128 I'm sure she'll be very
recognizable, since I've already created the tile
modulo the backdrop, just not yet grabbed the
backdrop and merged it into the appropriate absurd
tile set.

I buffed her up not to look ridiculous, by widening
the aspect ratio by about a third; _this_ Britney
looks like she could use that long sword to hack the
head off a master mind flayer without breaking
stride. I prefer women who don't look like they'd
snap in a strong wind, and since I'm making the
rules, that's what she is.

The hardest part, as always, was the hours spent
staring at Britney, deciding pixel by pixel "Britney
or Backdrop?" to cut away the clutter around her in
the image. Purest torture.

Gotta love The GIMP.

xanthian, fond of females.



